# Tile border colour (PR #14)

## Decisions (user chose, Oct 2026)

- Both: a theme-wide default and a per-tile override. The default is the theme's existing `card_edge` role (black in RPI dark); there is no new role.
- The per-tile value is a key, not a hex: a pastel or role key, picked from `INK_SWATCHES` like free-form `style.borderColor`. Null means the theme's card edge.

## Where it lives

- Model: `Tile.borderColor: String?` in `shared/.../Layout.kt`, mirrored as `borderColor?: string` in `editor/src/model/types.ts`. Optional, so old layouts load unchanged.
- Server: `Tiles.kt` draws the 2dp edge as the card's background behind its padding. `private fun DocContext.edgeOf(tile)` = `tile.borderColor?.let { paint(it) } ?: role(Role.CARD_EDGE)`. `paint` is the internal key resolver in `FreeForm.kt` (pastel first, then role).
- Edge-to-edge tiles (`kind == "home"`, or `full` weather/climate — `Tile.edgeToEdge()`) have no card, so no border. `TileDrawer.vue` hides the control for them with a matching `edgeToEdge` computed.
- Editor control: "Border colour" row under "Colour" in `TileDrawer.vue`, `ColorSwatches` with `clear-title="The theme's card edge"`.
- Editor preview: `GridMockup.vue` `place()` adds an inline `borderColor: colorOf(key)` over `.tile { border: 2px solid var(--rc-card-edge) }`. The selected-tile highlight is an `outline`, so it doesn't clash.
- Themes: `ThemesView.vue` labels `card_edge` "card edge (tile border)" with a hint above Roles. Built-in themes still have to be duplicated before their roles can be edited.

## Gotchas

- detekt (CI job "Server, shared and player") uses `server/detekt-baseline.xml`; baselined `MaxLineLength` entries match the exact line, so editing a long line re-checks it against the default 120 characters. `fun DocContext.tile` in `Tiles.kt` sits at the 60-line `LongMethod` limit, so splitting a line there fails too — move logic into a helper instead (that's why `edgeOf` exists).
- Run the CI job's steps locally before pushing: `./gradlew :shared:detekt :server:detekt :player:detekt :shared:test :server:test :player:testDebugUnitTest :player:lintDebug :player:assembleDebug`.
- No Node.js on the Mac, so the editor build (`vue-tsc --noEmit && vite build`) only runs in CI's "Editor" job.
- A commit hook adds `Co-authored-by: Cursor`; strip it before pushing (see the no-cursor-attribution rule).

## Not verified

Not checked by hand in the editor or on a tablet: setting a tile's border to a pastel, clearing it back to the theme's card edge, and changing `card_edge` in a custom theme.
